    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0447" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/922b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-22">June 22, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1617. Exchange negotiations—Far East. Department’s 1445, June 4. Assurances of
                    safe conduct for voyage of <hi rendition="#italic">Asama Maru</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Conte Verde</hi> between Japan and Lourenço Marques and
                    return have been received from governments of Belgium, China, Costa Rica, Cuba,
                    Czechoslovakia, Dominican Republic, Great Britain, Greece, Guatemala, Haiti,
                    Honduras, the Netherlands, Nicaragua, Norway, Panama, Poland, El Salvador,
                    Soviet Union, Yugoslavia.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d367-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="57" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
                <p>Department’s telegram No. 1662, June 29, to the Minister in Switzerland, added
                    the Mexican Government (390.1115A/948a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
